## ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: OpenCode Console v2 Browser Login Capture
The system SHALL launch the browser to `https://opencode.ai/console/login?next=%2Fconsole%2Fgo` and capture both the `opencode.ai` session cookies (including `__Host-console_session`) and the active workspace/organization identifier (`org_[a-zA-Z0-9]+` or `wrk_[a-zA-Z0-9]+`).

#### Scenario: Capturing org_ or wrk_ identifier from Console URL
- **WHEN** user completes login and the browser navigates to `https://opencode.ai/console/org_01JXYZ/go` or `https://opencode.ai/console/wrk_01JXYZ/go`
- **THEN** system extracts `org_01JXYZ` or `wrk_01JXYZ` as the WorkspaceID and captures the `opencode.ai` cookies

#### Scenario: Resolving WorkspaceID via Console Orgs API when URL has no ID
- **WHEN** user logs in and the browser stays on an authenticated `opencode.ai/console` page without an explicit `org_` or `wrk_` segment in the URL
- **THEN** system queries `GET https://opencode.ai/console/api/orgs` using the captured session cookies to resolve the primary organization ID

### Requirement: OpenCode Console v2 Account Page Restoration
The system SHALL inject saved OpenCode cookies via CDP (preserving host-only semantics for `__Host-` prefixed cookies) and navigate the account browser to `https://opencode.ai/console/<workspaceID>/go`.

#### Scenario: Opening OpenCode Console account page
- **WHEN** user triggers `open-page opencode <name>` or clicks the account card in the sidebar
- **THEN** system injects the saved cookies into the browser session and navigates to `https://opencode.ai/console/<workspaceID>/go`
## ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: OpenCode Console v2 JSON Quota Response Parsing
The system SHALL parse the OpenCode Console v2 `GET /console/api/go/status` JSON response, extracting `fiveHour` (mapped to `Rolling`), `week` (mapped to `Weekly`), and `month` (mapped to `Monthly`) meters from `access.meters`. Each meter SHALL compute `UsagePercent` from `usedMicroCents` and `limitMicroCents`, and compute `ResetInSec` and `ResetDisplay` relative to `resetsAt`.

#### Scenario: Active subscription with three usage meters
- **WHEN** `/console/api/go/status` returns a JSON object with non-null `access` containing `meters.fiveHour`, `meters.week`, and `meters.month` with valid non-negative integer strings for `usedMicroCents` and positive integer strings for `limitMicroCents`
- **THEN** the parser returns a `QuotaData` with `Rolling`, `Weekly`, and `Monthly` populated with accurate usage percentages and non-negative reset durations

#### Scenario: Lapsed or unsubscribed account returns null payload or null access
- **WHEN** `/console/api/go/status` returns literal `null` or a JSON object whose `access` field is `null`
- **THEN** the parser returns a `QuotaData` with `Lapsed: true` and `unavailable` status on `Rolling` and `Weekly`

#### Scenario: Five-hour rolling window has not started yet
- **WHEN** `access.meters.fiveHour` has `resetsAt: null` and `usedMicroCents: "0"` (before first use in the 5-hour window)
- **THEN** the parser accepts the meter with `ResetInSec: 0` and `UsagePercent: 0` without failing

#### Scenario: Malformed or negative micro-cents values fail closed
- **WHEN** `/console/api/go/status` returns negative `usedMicroCents`, zero or negative `limitMicroCents`, non-numeric strings, or missing required meter objects (`fiveHour` or `week`)
- **THEN** parsing fails closed with a descriptive error and fabricates no quota metrics
